{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01D7TgrXxRGWHqGg3G6maWwT","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# BUILD DISPOSITION of 009-CRITIQUE U5 — c67e85b\n2\t\n3\tWI-272 (dashboard work-item status fidelity, M-2 in\n4\t`docs/repo-review-2026-07-22.md`) is built and Review-A APPROVED (008-REVIEW-A,\n5\tfindings=0). This records the builder disposition of the sole outstanding\n6\tcritique finding, **U5** (009-CRITIQUE): it is **out of scope for WI-272** and\n7\tbelongs to a new owner-decided WI. WI-272 is left complete; no code change is\n8\tmade in this session.\n9\t\n10\t## WI-272 deliverable — verified complete\n11\t\n12\tThe six-state lifecycle (`queued|active|done|deferred|blocked|retired`) now\n13\tsurvives into every When-tab render surface:\n14\t\n15\t- `STATUS_FILL` + the `--deferred`/`--blocked` CSS vars carry `deferred`\n16\t  (`#6b21a8`) and `blocked` (`#b91c1c`);\n17\t- `STATUS_GLYPH` pairs each with a shape-distinct A3 glyph (deferred ▽,\n18\t  blocked ◼);\n19\t- the When legend lists both with their meanings (parked / impediment);\n20\t- the detail-panel badge colour is emitted straight from `STATUS_FILL`\n21\t  (`$status_color`), so it cannot drift from the vocabulary — the exact\n22\t  hand-kept four-state copy that was the M-2 defect;\n23\t- the flat-DAG fallback routes through the single `_wi_st` clamp helper, so no\n24\t  second inline copy can re-drop deferred/blocked.\n25\t\n26\tBoth new fills are byte-distinct from every other dashboard palette\n27\t(`STATUS_FILL` / `TIER_FILL` / `OKF_TYPE_FILL` / `PHASE_ACCENTS` /\n28\t`SW_NODE_FILL`) and clear WCAG AA under white label text (deferred 8.7:1,\n29\tblocked 6.5:1).\n30\t\n31\tEvidence (main-repo `.venv`, Python 3.11.9):\n32\t\n33\t- `gen_trajectory.py --root . --check` → `project-state dashboard up to date.`\n34\t- targeted fidelity tests — **6 passed**:\n35\t  `test_deferred_and_blocked_render_their_own_buckets`,\n36\t  `test_status_render_vocabulary_cannot_drift_from_the_registry_lifecycle`,\n37\t  `test_a3_status_glyph_pairs_every_status_fill`,\n38\t  `test_a3_flat_dag_fallback_also_prefixes_the_status_glyph`,\n39\t  `test_every_multifill_panel_emits_a_palette_bijection_legend`, module-size\n40\t  ratchet.\n41\t- `check_trajectory --strict`: the only render-related red is the **by-design**\n42\t  `perceptual-stale SR-052;SR-053;SR-054` gate, which holds until an independent\n43\t  post-integration critique lands (the render→re-fire→re-critique→clear steady\n44\t  state; cf. `docs/reviews/112-CRITIQUE.md`). The remaining reds are **WI-275**\n45\t  root-coordination-truth (status.md token / SpecRef archival) that the\n46\t  integrator scrubs at composition — not WI-272.\n47\t\n48\t## Why U5 is out of scope\n49\t\n50\tU5 asks to *\"declare disjoint palette tokens for status, phase, and type/tier,\n51\tmove the colliding Test Case/SR/SN or phase accents to non-overlapping hue\n52\tfamilies, and regenerate every affected node and legend\"* — routed to **@owner**.\n53\t\n54\t- The collisions U5 names are **pre-existing and systemic**, not introduced by\n55\t  WI-272: status `done` `#047857` == Test Case type `#047857` (What/Knowledge\n56\t  tabs); status `active` `#b45309` == Process Guide type `#b45309`; phase\n57\t  accents share hue families with the type palette. WI-272 touched none of\n58\t  `TIER_FILL` / `OKF_TYPE_FILL` / `PHASE_ACCENTS`.\n59\t- WI-272's own additions introduce **no** byte-identical collision: `#6b21a8`\n60\t  and `#b91c1c` are absent from every other palette (verified by grep of\n61\t  `gen_trajectory.py`).\n62\t- The remedy U5 asks for is a **cross-tab palette-token refactor** spanning the\n63\t  What, When, and Knowledge tabs and reassigning established semantic type\n64\t  colours — a design decision explicitly routed to @owner, not \"preserve\n65\t  deferred/blocked status.\"\n66\t\n67\tPer the repo's own pattern (M-2 → WI-272, M-3 → WI-273) and the\n68\t`render-dashboard-critique` skill (\"file findings as their own WIs\"), **U5 must\n69\tbecome a new owner-decided dashboard-palette-uniformity WI.** Expanding WI-272\n70\tto redesign the palette would be scope creep and would itself require a fresh\n71\trender critique. Hand-off, not fix.\n72\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8b6d1c3-0187-44c4-999a-954083d47644","uuid":"5ae11afa-d019-4289-aa98-d5d782a3efc3","timestamp":"2026-07-24T03:58:06.189Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Projects\\ai-template-trains\\1-g3-WI-272-230f\\docs\\reviews\\1-g3-WI-272-230f\\010-BUILD-DISPOSITION-c67e85b.md","content":"# BUILD DISPOSITION of 009-CRITIQUE U5 — c67e85b\n\nWI-272 (dashboard work-item status fidelity, M-2 in\n`docs/repo-review-2026-07-22.md`) is built and Review-A APPROVED (008-REVIEW-A,\nfindings=0). This records the builder disposition of the sole outstanding\ncritique finding, **U5** (009-CRITIQUE): it is **out of scope for WI-272** and\nbelongs to a new owner-decided WI. WI-272 is left complete; no code change is\nmade in this session.\n\n## WI-272 deliverable — verified complete\n\nThe six-state lifecycle (`queued|active|done|deferred|blocked|retired`) now\nsurvives into every When-tab render surface:\n\n- `STATUS_FILL` + the `--deferred`/`--blocked` CSS vars carry `deferred`\n  (`#6b21a8`) and `blocked` (`#b91c1c`);\n- `STATUS_GLYPH` pairs each with a shape-distinct A3 glyph (deferred ▽,\n  blocked ◼);\n- the When legend lists both with their meanings (parked / impediment);\n- the detail-panel badge colour is emitted straight from `STATUS_FILL`\n  (`$status_color`), so it cannot drift from the vocabulary — the exact\n  hand-kept four-state copy that was the M-2 defect;\n- the flat-DAG fallback routes through the single `_wi_st` clamp helper, so no\n  second inline copy can re-drop deferred/blocked.\n\nBoth new fills are byte-distinct from every other dashboard palette\n(`STATUS_FILL` / `TIER_FILL` / `OKF_TYPE_FILL` / `PHASE_ACCENTS` /\n`SW_NODE_FILL`) and clear WCAG AA under white label text (deferred 8.7:1,\nblocked 6.5:1).\n\nEvidence (main-repo `.venv`, Python 3.11.9):\n\n- `gen_trajectory.py --root . --check` → `project-state dashboard up to date.`\n- targeted fidelity tests — **6 passed**:\n  `test_deferred_and_blocked_render_their_own_buckets`,\n  `test_status_render_vocabulary_cannot_drift_from_the_registry_lifecycle`,\n  `test_a3_status_glyph_pairs_every_status_fill`,\n  `test_a3_flat_dag_fallback_also_prefixes_the_status_glyph`,\n  `test_every_multifill_panel_emits_a_palette_bijection_legend`, module-size\n  ratchet.\n- `check_trajectory --strict`: the only render-related red is the **by-design**\n  `perceptual-stale SR-052;SR-053;SR-054` gate, which holds until an independent\n  post-integration critique lands (the render→re-fire→re-critique→clear steady\n  state; cf. `docs/reviews/112-CRITIQUE.md`). The remaining reds are **WI-275**\n  root-coordination-truth (status.md token / SpecRef archival) that the\n  integrator scrubs at composition — not WI-272.\n\n## Why U5 is out of scope\n\nU5 asks to *\"declare disjoint palette tokens for status, phase, and type/tier,\nmove the colliding Test Case/SR/SN or phase accents to non-overlapping hue\nfamilies, and regenerate every affected node and legend\"* — routed to **@owner**.\n\n- The collisions U5 names are **pre-existing and systemic**, not introduced by\n  WI-272: status `done` `#047857` == Test Case type `#047857` (What/Knowledge\n  tabs); status `active` `#b45309` == Process Guide type `#b45309`; phase\n  accents share hue families with the type palette. WI-272 touched none of\n  `TIER_FILL` / `OKF_TYPE_FILL` / `PHASE_ACCENTS`.\n- WI-272's own additions introduce **no** byte-identical collision: `#6b21a8`\n  and `#b91c1c` are absent from every other palette (verified by grep of\n  `gen_trajectory.py`).\n- The remedy U5 asks for is a **cross-tab palette-token refactor** spanning the\n  What, When, and Knowledge tabs and reassigning established semantic type\n  colours — a design decision explicitly routed to @owner, not \"preserve\n  deferred/blocked status.\"\n\nPer the repo's own pattern (M-2 → WI-272, M-3 → WI-273) and the\n`render-dashboard-critique` skill (\"file findings as their own WIs\"), **U5 must\nbecome a new owner-decided dashboard-palette-uniformity WI.** Expanding WI-272\nto redesign the palette would be scope creep and would itself require a fresh\nrender critique. Hand-off, not fix.\n","numLines":72,"startLine":1,"totalLines":72}}}
