 the worker contract forbids editing coordination truth, a new `queued` row would force a forbidden `PROJECT_STATE.html` regen (or break `gen_trajectory --check`), WI-number assignment is a known cross-train collision hazard, and an uncited `docs/specs` file would trip R-F.\n\n## Why I didn't file the row / close the WI myself\n\nBoth actions are outside a train worker's authority and are exactly what the `@owner`-routed findings ask the owner/integrator to do. Attempting either on this branch would violate the coordination-truth prohibition or break the green bar. The residual pipeline (owner files U5 → independent post-integration critique APPROVEs → integrator flips WI-272→done) is the normal render→re-fire→re-critique→clear steady state.\n\n## Verification (main-repo `.venv`, Python 3.11.9)\n- `gen_trajectory.py --check` → up to date; full pre-commit G3 gate battery PASS.\n- Targeted fidelity tests: 5 passed; `test_module_size_ratchet.py`: 1 passed.\n- `check_trajectory --strict`: only render red is the by-construction `perceptual-stale` gate; the other reds are WI-275 root-coordination-truth the integrator scrubs.\n\nI did not run the full smoke tier because the diff is a single review-markdown file with no code or test surface; I ran the relevant targeted tests plus the complete pre-commit gate battery instead, all green."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2777,"cache_read_input_tokens":130427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2777},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8b6d1c3-0187-44c4-999a-954083d47644","uuid":"704c3227-8480-4737-a593-063936590a48","request_id":"req_011CdLEMzPPYwfqJb9613weS"}
